assertion  XSH.towupper.001
anchor     functions/towupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/towupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale towupper() maps each of the 26 lowercase
           letters to the corresponding uppercase letter.
test       t/001-mapping.c

assertion  XSH.towupper.002
anchor     functions/towupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/towupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       towupper() returns the other portable characters unchanged: the
           uppercase letters, the digits, the punctuation, the space and the
           control characters.
test       t/002-unchanged.c

assertion  XSH.towupper.003
anchor     functions/towupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/towupper.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       towupper(WEOF) returns WEOF (an argument of the domain with no
           mapping is returned unchanged).
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.towupper.004
anchor     functions/towupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/towupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       For each lowercase letter c, towlower(towupper(c)) equals c and the
           result of towupper(c) is a uppercase letter in the class sense
           (iswupper or iswlower as appropriate).
test       t/004-round-trip.c
